{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-data-bucket"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-data-bucket/*"
    }
  ]
}

Attach as a customer managed policy: go to IAM → Policies → Create policy, paste JSON, name it 'S3ReadMyDataBucket'. Then go to Roles → find the Lambda's execution role → Attach policies → select the new policy.

Using a customer managed policy allows you to reuse it across multiple functions and version it. Inline policies are embedded directly in a single role and can be harder to track.
